          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.31.38",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.31.38",
      "verse": 38,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "These twenty years ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "have",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "been",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with thee: thy ewes and thy she-goats have not cast their young, and the rams of thy flock have I not eaten.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.31.39",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.31.39",
      "verse": 39,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That which was torn by beasts, I brought not to thee; I bore the loss of it; of my hand didst thou require it, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "whether",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " stolen by day, or stolen by night.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.31.40",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.31.40",
      "verse": 40,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thus",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I was; in the day the drouth consumed me, and the frost by night; and my sleep departed from my eyes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.31.41",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.31.41",
      "verse": 41,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thus have I been twenty years in thy house: I served thee fourteen years for thy two daughters, and six years for thy cattle: and thou hast changed my wages ten times.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.31.42",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.31.42",
      "verse": 42,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Except the God of my father, the God of Abraham, and the fear of Isaac had been with me, surely thou hadst now sent me away empty. God hath seen my affliction, and the labor of my hands, and rebuked ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thee",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " yesternight.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.31.43",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.31.43",
      "verse": 43,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Laban answered, and said to Jacob, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "These",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " daughters ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my daughters, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "these",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " children ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my children, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "these",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " cattle ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my cattle, and all that thou seest ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mine; and what can I do this day to these my daughters, or to their children which they have borne?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.31.44",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.31.44",
      "verse": 44,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now therefore come thou, let us make a covenant, I and thou; and let it be for a witness between me and thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.31.45",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.31.45",
      "verse": 45,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Jacob took a stone, and set it up ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a pillar.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.31.46",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.31.46",
      "verse": 46,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Jacob said to his brethren, Gather stones; and they took stones, and made a heap: and they ate there upon the heap.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.31.47",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.31.47",
      "verse": 47,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Laban called it Jegar-sahadutha: but Jacob called it Galeed:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.31.48",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.31.48",
      "verse": 48,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Laban said, This heap ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a witness between me and thee this day. Therefore was the name of it called Galeed:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.31.49",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.31.49",
      "verse": 49,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Mizpah; for he said, The LORD watch between me and thee, when we are absent one from another.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.31.50",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.31.50",
      "verse": 50,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If thou shalt afflict my daughters, or if thou shalt take ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "other",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wives besides my daughters; no man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with us; See, God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " witness betwixt me and thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.31.51",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.31.51",
      "verse": 51,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Laban said to Jacob, Behold this heap, and behold ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "this",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " pillar, which I have cast betwixt me and thee;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.31.52",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.31.52",
      "verse": 52,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This heap ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " witness, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "this",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " pillar ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " witness, that I will not pass over this heap to thee, and that thou shalt not pass over this heap and this pillar to me, for harm.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.31.53",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.31.53",
      "verse": 53,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The God of Abraham, and the God of Nahor, the God of their father, judge betwixt us. And Jacob swore by the fear of his father Isaac.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
